.* QTOCCFG: CFGTCP, the TCP/IP configuration menu, with its related
.* tables menu (option 21) and the point-to-point menu (option 22,
.* CFGTCPPTP). The driver is work/qsjob/src/panels/tcp/; a RETURN
.* option is a list it shows, a CMD option a command it runs.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='CFGTCP'.
:IMPORT NAME=CFGTCPAPP PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=CFGTCPPTP PNLGRP=QHTOCPPCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=CHGTCPA PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=CHGTCPDMN PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=MRGTCPHT PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKNETTBLE PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKPCLTBLE PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKSRVTBLE PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS' NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTCP HELP=HLPCFG KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Configure TCP/IP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT1' OPTION=1 ACTION='RETURN 101'.Work with TCP/IP interfaces
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT2' OPTION=2 ACTION='RETURN 102'.Work with TCP/IP routes
:MENUI HELP=CHGTCPA OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?CHGTCPA'.Change TCP/IP attributes
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT4' OPTION=4 ACTION='RETURN 104'.Work with TCP/IP port restrictions
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT10' OPTION=10 ACTION='RETURN 110'.Work with TCP/IP host table entries
:MENUI HELP=MRGTCPHT OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?MRGTCPHT'.Merge TCP/IP host table
:MENUI HELP=CHGTCPDMN OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD ?CHGTCPDMN'.Change TCP/IP domain information
:MENUI HELP=CFGTCPAPP OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPAPP'.Configure TCP/IP applications
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT21' OPTION=21 ACTION='RETURN 121'.Configure related tables
:MENUI HELP=CFGTCPPTP OPTION=22 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPPTP'.Configure point-to-point TCP/IP
:MENUI HELP='CFGTCP/OPT23' OPTION=23 ACTION='RETURN 123'.Load/Unload IP Filter
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTBL HELP=HLPTBL KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure Related Tables
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI HELP=WRKSRVTBLE OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSRVTBLE'.Work with service table entries
:MENUI HELP=WRKPCLTBLE OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKPCLTBLE'.Work with protocol table entries
:MENUI HELP=WRKNETTBLE OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD WRKNETTBLE'.Work with network table entries
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGPTP HELP=HLPPTP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure Point-to-Point TCP/IP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI HELP='CFGPTP/OPT2' OPTION=2 ACTION='RETURN 202'.Work with active point-to-point jobs
:MENUGRP.Modem information options
:MENUI HELP='CFGPTP/OPT11' OPTION=11 ACTION='RETURN 211'.Work with modem information
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Other related options:
:MENUI HELP='CFGPTP/OPT21' OPTION=21 ACTION='RETURN 221'.Work with PPP line descriptions
:MENUI HELP='CFGPTP/OPT22' OPTION=22 ACTION='RETURN 222'.Work with PPP line description status
:EMENUGRP.
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPCFG.Configure TCP/IP - Help
:P.Everything TCP/IP uses: the interfaces with their addresses, the routes,
the stack's attributes, the ports kept for chosen user profiles, the host
table, the local names and the name servers, the applications and the
tables of services, protocols and networks.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to where you were.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPTBL.Configure Related Tables - Help
:P.The services table names the ports of well-known services; the
protocol and network tables name protocols and networks. Programs look
names up in them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPPTP.Configure Point-to-Point TCP/IP - Help
:P.Point-to-point profiles connect over modems and PPP lines, which this
release does not have.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT1'.Work with TCP/IP interfaces
:P.Option 1. Work with TCP/IP interfaces.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT2'.Work with TCP/IP routes
:P.Option 2. Work with TCP/IP routes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT4'.Work with TCP/IP port restrictions
:P.Option 4. Work with TCP/IP port restrictions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT10'.Work with TCP/IP host table entries
:P.Option 10. Work with TCP/IP host table entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT21'.Configure related tables
:P.Option 21. Configure related tables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCP/OPT23'.Load/Unload IP Filter
:P.Option 23. Load/Unload IP Filter.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGPTP/OPT2'.Work with active point-to-point jobs
:P.Option 2. Work with active point-to-point jobs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGPTP/OPT11'.Work with modem information
:P.Option 11. Work with modem information.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGPTP/OPT21'.Work with PPP line descriptions
:P.Option 21. Work with PPP line descriptions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGPTP/OPT22'.Work with PPP line description status
:P.Option 22. Work with PPP line description status.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
